# .dockerignore — Default exclusions for the Docker build context.
#
# Goal: keep every build context small, safe, and free of secrets.
#
# SCOPE
# -----
# This is the shared baseline.  It is the effective policy for Dockerfile.mlflow
# (which has no specific ignore file) and for any builder that does not support
# per-Dockerfile ignore files — notably the legacy, non-BuildKit builder.  The
# two serving images additionally declare stricter, image-specific contexts:
#
#   Dockerfile.api.dockerignore        — source + params + verified bundle only
#   Dockerfile.dashboard.dockerignore  — source + static demo assets only
#
# BuildKit uses the Dockerfile-specific file INSTEAD OF this one (they are not
# merged), so all three files are self-contained.  Those two express a
# separation this shared file cannot: the API context must carry no dataset,
# and the dashboard context must carry no model or bundle.
#
# STRATEGY
# --------
# Deny everything, then re-include the union of what the three Dockerfiles
# actually copy.  The working tree is several hundred megabytes (mlruns/ alone
# is ~367 MB); an allow-list keeps that out by construction rather than by
# remembering to exclude each new artifact directory.
#
# Dockerfile.mlflow copies only docker/init_mlflow.sh — the canonical database
# is bind-mounted read-only at runtime, never baked into an image.

# ── Deny everything ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**

# ── Application source and packaging (all images) ────────────────────────────
!src/
!params.yaml
!pyproject.toml
!docker/
!.streamlit/
!.env.example

# ── Dedicated runtime dependency manifests ───────────────────────────────────
# The serving images install ONLY these, never the full requirements.txt.  That
# file is the development/MLOps environment (MLflow, DVC, Evidently, shap,
# pytest, ruff) and is used by CI and the Makefile on the host, not in an image
# — so it is deliberately NOT re-included and cannot reach any build context.
# Dockerfile.mlflow pins `mlflow>=3.14,<4` inline and copies no manifest at all.
!requirements-api.txt
!requirements-dashboard.txt

# ── API image: the checksum-verified champion bundle ─────────────────────────
!deploy/bundles/

# ── Dashboard image: read-only synthetic demonstration assets ────────────────
# Restored by `dvc pull` in CI before the build.  Parent directories must be
# re-included too, or Docker will not descend into them.
!data/
!data/raw/
!data/raw/observations.csv
!models/
!models/evaluation_health.json
!models/evaluation_restoration.json
!reports/
!reports/drift_summary.json

# ── Re-exclusions: never let the rules above pull these back in ──────────────
# Version control and DVC metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.dvc/
.dvcignore

# DVC cache (large, never needed in a container)
.dvc/cache/
.dvc/tmp/

# Secrets — must never enter any build context
.env
**/.env
.dvc/config.local
*.pem
*.key

# Virtual environments (dependencies are installed inside the image)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Trained artefacts: models are served from deploy/bundles/, never copied loose
models/*.joblib
data/processed/
data/reference/
data/production/

# MLflow database and runs — mounted at runtime by the mlflow service only
artifacts/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
mlflow.db

# Full Evidently HTML reports (large; page 8 only checks whether they exist)
reports/*.html

# Python caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
coralsense_mlops.egg-info/

# Tests, notebooks and documentation are not needed in serving images
tests/
notebooks/
docs/

# Test caches and coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# CI temp artefacts
ci_mlruns.db
ci_check_mlruns.db

# Log files
*.log
logs/

# Local editor, OS and assistant files
.idea/
.vscode/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/
